[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2569288315","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101071#issuecomment-2569288315","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101071","id":2569288315,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZJDp7","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-03T14:19:49Z","updated_at":"2025-01-03T14:19:49Z","body":"I'd be curious to hear your take on this @jrouwe, and whether you think it's worthwhile to begin with.\r\n\r\nI'm personally so used to seeing this type of container be used in larger game-related codebases that I didn't even bother to do any profiling when making this same change to the extension, and I must admit the improvements were not as drastic as I had imagined. But again, that probably depends greatly on the platform/machine as well.\r\n\r\nThe fact that Godot fairly liberally allocates memory elsewhere (through the default system allocator) does make this change seem a bit \"against the grain\" though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2569288315/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2569350901","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101071#issuecomment-2569350901","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101071","id":2569350901,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZJS71","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-03T14:53:10Z","updated_at":"2025-01-03T14:53:10Z","body":"I suppose it's also worth discussing whether this should even be its own container or instead just a custom allocator. Ideally it would be a custom allocator for `LocalVector`, perhaps even added to `core/templates/`, but `LocalVector` doesn't support custom allocators (nor aligned allocations) at the moment, so it would have to be for `JPH::Array` instead.\r\n\r\nHowever, I did find the custom `std::allocator` that I used in the extension to be quite messy with its various configurations and gotchas, and not much shorter than this container implementation, hence why I went with this more straight-forward approach. Obviously you lose out on a lot of the methods with this custom container though, so in a more general setting it would likely balloon in size quite quickly.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2569350901/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2569911714","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101071#issuecomment-2569911714","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101071","id":2569911714,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZLb2i","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-03T22:56:52Z","updated_at":"2025-01-04T12:47:23Z","body":"I think avoiding memory allocations is very useful and a good way to speed things up!\r\n\r\nA custom allocator was indeed what I was thinking about too and I thought it would be fun to write one:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/pull/1435\r\n\r\nTurns out it wasn't fun at all, mainly because Jolt can fall back to using `std::vector` when `JPH_USE_STD_VECTOR` is defined and the rebind logic is not fun with an allocator like this.\r\n\r\nEdit: The PR has been merged now, feel free to use this allocator or to use what you have already written.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2569911714/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571317423","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101071#issuecomment-2571317423","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101071","id":2571317423,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZQzCv","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-04T14:19:58Z","updated_at":"2025-01-04T14:19:58Z","body":"> Turns out it wasn't fun at all, mainly because Jolt can fall back to using `std::vector` when `JPH_USE_STD_VECTOR` is defined and the rebind logic is not fun with an allocator like this.\r\n\r\nYeah, that looks about as fun as I remember it being. 😅 I'm glad you caught both the rebinding and non-stateless gotchas.\r\n\r\nI appreciate the addition though. I'm not sure I can justify bumping Jolt just for this, but I suppose we could switch to your `STLLocalAllocator` once we do, whether that's before or after this is merged.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571317423/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571318607","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101071#issuecomment-2571318607","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101071","id":2571318607,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZQzVP","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-04T14:25:02Z","updated_at":"2025-01-04T14:25:02Z","body":"You could also only add `STLLocalAllocator.h` and not upgrade the rest as it doesn't depend on any other changes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571318607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651127261","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101071#issuecomment-2651127261","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101071","id":2651127261,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eBP3d","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T15:16:52Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T15:16:52Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651127261/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":5,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]